WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.610 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  Sniper Elite games are about perching  yourself in a bombed-out tower pulling a  trigger and watching a bullet careen  through nazi flesh-and-bone these skull  shattering bone destroying kill shots  make the series a devilish joy but where  the series has regularly faltered is in  the moments in between these euphoric  long-range kills  however with Sniper Elite for developer  rebellion has changed all that  Sniper Elite for features expansive  sandbox is brimming with open-ended  objectives that you can choose to  complete in any way you desire and in  any order you please each one is set in  a variety of varied locales stretching  across picturesque Italian landscapes on  the verge of invasion and each one of  its locales is teeming with fascists  just waiting to be extinguished with a  well-placed bullet collectibles and  advantageous sniping positions are  judiciously dotted around each map  encouraging you to explore and find  opportunities pots the macabre  satisfaction of sniping is increased  tenfold when you're able to execute a  pinpoint headshot from as far as 400  meters away of course Sniper Elite  signature x-ray kills return in all  their morbid glory and the series is  grisly ballistics are still second to  none it might sound a bit tasteless but  there's something wonderfully schlocky  about rupturing an enemy scrotum from  200 metres away  [Music]  getting into fruitful sniping positions  isn't the choy once was either there's a  newfound responsiveness to protagonist  Carl fair burns movement that makes it  easier to get around and stay hidden and  there's a decent degree of verticality  each map as you now have the ability to  clamber up specific surfaces jump across  gaps and climb in and out of windows to  navigate with increased freedom if  you're spotted and the bullets start  flying pulling out your thompson and  going toe-to-toe with bloodthirsty  fascists isn't as clunky or as  frustrating as it used to be  while his cover based shooting is merely  competent at best its viability as a  messy plan be for when things go awry is  very much appreciated and since every  objective essentially occupies a pocket  of space on the map you can cause as  much mayhem and destruction as you  please without worrying about enemies  being on high alert for the rest of the  mission the AI in Sniper Elite 4 shows  an improvement over its predecessors  enemies attempt to triangulate your  position based on the sound of gunfire  and officers will command their over  troops to overwhelm you if they have  your location locked down inconsistency  is a common minister and they're not  always the brightest Bunch there were a  number of occasions where I would simply  circle around an area after being  spotted only to find a bundle of enemies  cowering behind cover near my last known  position with all their backs turned it  was easy pickings if you want a harder  challenge from the occasional bungling  enemy the authentic difficulty setting  strips away all of the handy assists and  extends the life of the campaign with a  steep learning curve you'll probably  want to skip all the cutscenes a second  time round though as the plot is  completely forgettable a stereotypical  world will to tell with an unhinged Nazi  villain and a super weapon only a gruff  American hero can stop some surface  level details touch on the Italian  resistance and the Mafia's role in the  war but it never delves deep enough to  be particularly enlightening or engaging  as a story  Luminos it's crucial we find out what  the Nazis are up to in terms of  multiplayer there are petra of game mode  spread across competitive and  cooperative offerings control asks a  team to battle for supremacy over an  ever moving control point disregarding  the sniper rifle in favor of some up  close and personal skirmishes this sits  in stark contrast to the rest of the  competitive modes which are  predominantly marksmen affairs  if you enjoy cautiously moving across  maps with an eye open for the glint of  an enemy scope then there's something  here for you killing a human player from  the opposite side of a map is immensely  satisfying but these moments are few and  far in between it was never enough to  hold my attention for too long  survival fairs much better as up to four  players work together to survive  increasingly challenging waves of  enemies a la horde mode as snipers  distance is the key advantage and is fun  finding an opportune location to seek  shelter and pick off each wave of  progressively difficult Nazis in a  unique twist the supply box are used to  replenish your ammunition also moves to  a different location every few waves  forcing you to get creative with your  trap placement and discover new areas to  camp out in once more or fire tanks and  heavily armoured units rain down upon  you it can get incredibly intense  Sniper Elite 4 feels like a natural  progression for the series as rebellion  continues to refine its systems and put  a greater emphasis on the long-range  shooting it does so well it's dolphin  action mechanics may be simplistic but  they're functional and regularly  enjoyable and the maps with the  impressive scale open-ended objectives  and clever level design coalesce these  disparate systems into a creative and  fulfilling whole there are still some  issues with AI inconsistency a bland  story and some dull competitive  multiplayer but it finally feels like  this series is living up to its  long-standing potential  [Music]  [Music]

